    "url": "components/fleet-agent.html#containers-from-templates",
    "text": "Specification 26.12. Instead of hand-made start and stop commands against a container someone created on the slave, a deployment row may say how to create it: { \"id\": \"rig-qwen\", \"host\": \"rig\", \"accelerator\": \"rig-gpu0\", \"run\": { \"image\": \"llama-server\", \"ports\": [{\"bind\": \"192.168.1.20\", \"host\": 8080, \"container\": 8080}], \"env\": [\"LLAMA_ARG_CTX_SIZE=131072\"], \"args\": [\"--model\", \"/state/qwen.gguf\", \"--port\", \"8080\"], \"state_path\": \"/state\" }, \"probe\": [\"curl\", \"-fsS\", \"--max-time\", \"5\", \"http://127.0.0.1:8080/health\"] } image names an artifact row, whose image field is the reference on the host (default: its id). The host must declare data_dir — an enrolled host carries the one it registered — and the container's state lives in <data_dir>/containers/<deployment-id>, mounted at state_path. The GPU is the accelerator row's index. The container is named hypellm-<deployment-id> unless container says otherwise, and start/stop default to docker start/docker stop of it. On ACTIVATE the agent creates the state directory, then the container if it is absent, labelled hypellm.template=<sha256> over the whole create command. A container whose label differs was made from an older row: it is removed with docker rm (never -f, so a running one is never removed) and created again. A template the shim would refuse — a deployment id that is not one plain path segment, a bind that is not an IPv4 address, an environment key that is not an identifier, a state path with .. — is refused when the file is loaded. The shim's docker create vocabulary is --name, the hypellm.template label, --gpus device=N, -p <IPv4>:<port>:<port>, -v <data_dir>/containers/<name>:<path>, -e KEY=VALUE and --restart no, then the image and the container's own arguments. Privileged mode, host networking or PID namespace, capabilities, devices, and any other mount are refused, so the agent's key cannot be turned into a root shell on the slave through docker create."
